course: dictionary
lesson: 3571
title: Fetch: one word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Fetch is a verb, so it shows an action. Its main meaning is to go and get something or someone, and bring them back. «Fetch the doctor» tells you to go and bring the doctor here.
explain: Context shows you which meaning is used. In «Her foster mum, Jan, takes one look and fetches a proper suitcase with wheels», fetches means goes and gets the suitcase and brings it back. Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence? Then test your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
explain: Fetch can also mean a price, and it is the name of a game. «The old car fetched 500 dollars» means the car was sold for that much money. When you play fetch with a dog, you throw a ball or stick and the dog brings it back.
fact: Fetch means to go and get something or someone and bring them back.
fact: «Fetches», «fetched» and «fetching» are different forms of the same verb.
fact: Fetch can mean to be sold for a certain price, as in «the old car fetched 500 dollars».
fact: Fetch is also a game, where a dog brings back a ball or stick you throw.
fact: «Far-fetched» means hard to believe, as in «a far-fetched story».
exercise: «The Dog came with a stick in his mouth to fetch and carry.» What does fetch mean here? | To sing loudly | *To go and bring things back | To fall asleep | To sell something
exercise: «The old car fetched 500 dollars.» What does fetched mean? | Went to get 500 dollars | Lost 500 dollars | Was painted red | *Was sold for 500 dollars
exercise: A dog brings back a ball that you throw. What is this game called? | *Fetch | Tag | Hide | Catch the moon
test: «Jan fetched a proper suitcase with wheels.» What does fetched mean in this sentence? | Painted | Threw away | *Went and got it and brought it back | Wrapped up
test: What does «far-fetched» mean? | *Hard to believe | Fast to run | Made of wood | Very far away
exam: Ali says, «Fetch the ball, good boy!» What is Ali asking the dog to do? | Dig a hole in the garden | Sleep in its bed | *Go and bring the ball back | Run away from the ball
